arguments.prompt:
You are building a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-d99d22089a0c430b962a399984675f22/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -au Individual -f net10.0`. It has two projects:

- **Server**: `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/` (the main ASP.NET Core host)
- **Client**: `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/` (the Blazor WebAssembly client)

The solution file is `ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.sln`.

## Requirements

1. **Dispatchers** view a list of shipments with status and destination
2. **Customers** check their shipment status and estimated delivery
3. Worldwide users — Auto render mode (already configured)
4. Fast first load, snappy after — Auto render mode handles this
5. Every page involves interactive controls — use `@rendermode InteractiveAuto`
6. Staff and customers authenticate with Individual accounts (already configured with Identity)

## What to implement

### 1. Shared Models (in Client project so both server and WASM can use them)

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 2. Server Data Model

Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [Required, MaxLength(20)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(50)]
    public string Status { get; set; } = "Pending";

    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }

    [Required, MaxLength(256)]
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(500)]
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 3. Update ApplicationDbContext

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
    public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
}
```

### 4. Add a new EF migration and update the database

Run from the server project directory:
```bash
cd /tmp/sv-d99d22089a0c430b962a399984675f22/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker
dotnet ef migrations add AddShipments
dotnet ef database update
```

### 5. Seed Data and Roles in Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`. After `var app = builder.Build();`, add a scope to seed roles and sample data. Add roles "Dispatcher" and "Customer". Seed ~8 sample shipments with varied statuses (Pending, In Transit, Out for Delivery, Delivered, Delayed). Use `app.Services.CreateScope()` pattern.

Here's the seeding code to add right after `var app = builder.Build();`:

```csharp
using (var scope = app.Services.CreateScope())
{
    var roleManager = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<RoleManager<IdentityRole>>();
    string[] roles = ["Dispatcher", "Customer"];
    foreach (var role in roles)
    {
        if (!await roleManager.RoleExistsAsync(role))
        {
            await roleManager.CreateAsync(new IdentityRole(role));
        }
    }

    var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContext>();
    if (!db.Shipments.Any())
    {
        db.Shipments.AddRange(
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-10001", Origin = "New York, NY", Destination = "Los Angeles, CA", Status = "In Transit", ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-3), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(2), CustomerEmail = "alice@example.com", Description = "Electronics - 2 boxes" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-10002", Origin = "Chicago, IL", Destination = "Miami, FL", Status = "Delivered", ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-7), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-2), ActualDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-2), CustomerEmail = "bob@example.com", Description = "Furniture - 1 pallet" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-10003", Origin = "Seattle, WA", Destination = "Denver, CO", Status = "Pending", ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow, EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(4), CustomerEmail = "carol@example.com", Description = "Medical supplies" },
            new Shipment { TrackingNumber = "TRK-10004", Origin = "Boston, MA", Destination = "Houston, TX", Status = "Out for Delivery", ShippedDate = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-5), EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow, CustomerEmail = "alice@example.com", Description = "Auto parts - 3 boxes" },
